<title>USA: ESCELSA Euro/144a bond deal postponed-sources.</title>
<headline>ESCELSA Euro/144a bond deal postponed-sources.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Espirito Santo Centrais Eletricas (ESCELSA) has postponed a $350 million Eurobond/144a private placement debt offering until next week due to volatilty in the markets for Brazilian securities, market sources said.</p>
<p>Officials at Morgan Stanley &amp; Co, the lead underwriter of the deal, declined to comment.  </p>
<p>ESCELSA, an electric utility in the territory of the state of Espirito Santo, planned to sell $350 million in senior unsecured notes due 2007 on Thursday.</p>
<p>The deal was rated B1/BB-minus.</p>
<p>Markets for Brazilian bonds and stocks were whipsawed this week as traders tried to determine whether recent Asian currency turmoil might affect the Brazilian real.</p>
<p>-Douglas Brown, U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1662</p>
